NAME
    for - iterate over a list of words

SYNOPSIS
    for NAME in word...; do LIST; done

DESCRIPTION
    Expands the word list (applying quoting, variable expansion, and
    command substitution), assigns each resulting word to NAME in turn,
    and executes LIST once per word.

    break(1) exits the loop early; continue(1) advances to the next word.
    All loop iterations share the shell's 10-second wall-clock safety
    timeout and check for interrupts between iterations.

EXAMPLES
    for i in 1 2 3; do echo $i; done
    for f in $(ls /Logs); do echo $f; done

EXIT STATUS
    0   The list was empty, or the last executed command in the loop body
        exited 0.
    N   Exit status of the last command executed in the loop body, or 130
        if interrupted.

SEE ALSO
    while(1), break(1), continue(1), if(1)
